     "form": "Mosaic",
     "style": "Middle Byzantine (Komnenian)",
     "summary": "Gazing down from the centre of the dome, this Christ Pantocrator — 'Ruler of All' — is among the most powerful images in Byzantine art: his eyes are searching and severe, his brow furrowed, his long fingers gripping a jewelled Gospel book. The dome placed Christ at the summit of the church as an image of heaven, watching over the whole of creation and the worshippers below.",
