     "summary": "Christ Pantocrator stands between the Virgin Mary and John the Baptist, who turn toward him in intercession for humanity on the Day of Judgment. Though the lower half has been lost, the surviving faces are among the most tender and lifelike in all Byzantine art, with soft modeling and an inward, sorrowful gentleness. It is generally thought to have been made to celebrate the recovery of Constantinople from Latin rule in 1261.",
